downloads/*.docx

# Everything the tool writes under logs/ is sensitive: the session cookie, the
# run logs (applicant names, and today a CTK value), the captured URLs (live
# CSRF tokens), and attach mode's chrome_profile/ — a persistent Chrome profile
# holding the live Indeed employer session, cookie DB and all.
#
# Ignore the directory rather than listing extensions. The previous rules were
# single-level globs (logs/*.log, logs/*.json), so logs/chrome_profile/Default/
# Cookies matched none of them and sat one `git add .` from a public fork. The
# next artifact dropped in here is ignored by default instead of by remembering.
logs/**

# Spec files
*.spec

# Keep folders
!downloads/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.config

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.cache

# Chrome driver
chromedriver.exe
chromedriver

# DevTools network captures from HR — contain bearer tokens + session cookies
indeed_graphql_*.txt

# Live Indeed session token — treat like a password (see HR_GUIDE.md security checklist)
indeed_cookies.json

# Screenshots from debugging sessions. These are taken over a live Indeed
# employer console, so they capture real applicant profiles — education,
# certifications, candidate IDs. This repo is a PUBLIC fork; a single
# `git add .` would publish them irreversibly.
*.png

# Run reports: job titles and counts, no applicant names, but no reason to
# ship them. logs/*.log and logs/*.json are already covered above; .txt is not.
download_report.txt
logs/*.txt

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace
.superpowers/
